{title: We Give Thee But Thine Own}
{artist: William W. How / William H. Monk}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (We_Give_Thee_But_Thine_Own-Energy)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]We give Thee [Am]but Thine [G]own,
[G]What[D]e’er [Bm]the [Em]gift [A]may [D]be;
[D]All [C]that we [G]have is Thine a[B]lone,
[G]A [Am]trust, O Lord, [D]from [G]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]May we Thy [Am]bounties [G]thus
[G]As [D]stew[Bm]ards [Em]true [A]re[D]ceive,
[D]And [C]gladly, [G]as Thou blessest [B]us,
[G]To [Am]Thee our first[D]fruits [G]give.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]O hearts are [Am]bruised and [G]dead,
[G]And [D]homes [Bm]are [Em]bare [A]and [D]cold,
[D]And [C]lambs for [G]whom the Shepherd [B]bled
[G]Are [Am]straying from [D]the [G]fold.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]To comfort [Am]and to [G]bless,
[G]To [D]find [Bm]a [Em]balm [A]for [D]woe,
[D]To [C]tend the [G]lone and father[B]less
[G]Is [Am]angels’ work [D]be[G]low.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]The captive [Am]to re[G]lease,
[G]To [D]God [Bm]the [Em]lost [A]to [D]bring,
[D]To [C]teach the [G]way of life and [B]peace—
[G]It [Am]is a Christ[D]-like [G]thing.
{end_of_verse}
